==Battleground==
*1 [[Mr. Puffington]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Rain D.]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Mr. Puffington]]s spawn, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
**5 [[Dolphina]]s spawn, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
A simple and easy, albeit slow way to defeat this stage is stacking [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunks]] on the first Puffington, as no other enemies spawn until the base is hit. If not doing this, make sure to take advantage of the fact that the enemies here have a lot of knockbacks.

====Recommended Units====
* [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] - With talents, Awakened Bahamut can keep pressure off of himself by continually knocking back enemies with Explosions. He can still be used to tear down Rain D. without talents.
* [[Dogumaru (Special Cat)|Reborn Warrior Doguemon]]: Dogumaru's [[True Form]] gains Relic targeting, and in tandem with his HP boost and Cooldown decrease, makes him a solid choice here. He can tank every enemy here well while doing good offense to slowly kill them. Assist him with units such as Slime Cat and Bullet Train Cat. He doesn't work well without his true form, as the Puffingtons can melt through his HP, making this unit only a solid choice for higher difficulties.
* [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi]] - At Level 37 or higher, Idi:N2 can survive a 100% Puffington hit; if Idi:N2 hits the base, it will end up dying after hitting the Puffington twice and killing it, making the initial fight much easier.
* [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Uril]] - Helps to knock back Dolphina and keep Puffington away from the front line.
* [[Wave Attack|Wave]]/[[Long Distance|LD]]/[[Surge Attack|Surge]] units - These can hit several enemies at once and potentially knock back all at the same time. Good examples are [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], and especially [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]].

==Trivia==
*Curry Comet is a pun on [[wikipedia:Halley's Comet|Halley's Comet]] that was lost in translation. In Japanese, Curry Comet is Karē Suisei (カレー彗星) while Halley's Comet is Harē Suisei (ハレー彗星)

